  "hindi": "क्या वह रीति, पुरानी या नई, हे देवियो, हे उषाओ, आज तुम्हारी हो, जिससे तुम धनवती देवियो ने नवग्व, अङ्गिरस्, दशग्व, सप्तास्य के लिए धन के साथ उदय किया।",
  "english": "Might that course of yours, old or new, be today, O goddesses, O Dawns, by which you, wealthy ones, dawned richly for Navagva, Aṅgiras, Daśagva, Saptāsya.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Syntax uncertain. kuvit is rendered \"might ... indeed\" with the precative babhūyāt; vaḥ is taken as genitive \"of you\". yena (src yenā, metrical lengthening) refers to the yāma (\"course\"). The four datives are names (Saptāsya may be an epithet \"seven-mouthed\"); aṅgire is read as a form of Aṅgiras/Aṅgira. ūṣa is read as 2 pl. perfect of √vas; this and the whole relative clause are tentative.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
